#
# 1. Apply patch in ~/lab/kernel/linux-6.6.9/
# 2. Build lib/dim/ and mlx5_core module only:
#       cd ~/lab/kernel/linux-6.6.9
#       make M=lib/dim modules
#       make M=drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core modules
#    (or rebuild full kernel if needed — net_dim_stats_compare is inline
#     in net_dim.c so vmlinux needs rebuild)
# 3. Install:
#       sudo rmmod mlx5_core; sudo modprobe mlx5_core  # NIC down/up
#    (only safe if you have console access — NIC reset)
# 4. Repeat measurement (Sec 12 of H1_analysis.md):
#       BITRATE=40G LEN_OPT="-l 9000" ~/lab/scripts/run_dim_cycle.sh on 30
#    Expected with patch: stack throughput 6.96 G → ~15-20 G (recovery via
#    DIM walking down profile_ix when drops increase).
